## Lessons

- **WTI 15m ≠ Yahoo CL=F:** Kalshi settles `KXWTI15M` on Pyth `Metal.XTI/USD`. Yahoo `CL=F` as live spot printed model 0.999 vs book 0.045 on a weekend. `yahoo_may_proxy_settlement` is gold/silver only; Hermes-down withholds WTI.
- **GOLDH trial cannot import the 15m lab:** `kxgoldh_forward_paper.py` must own `batch_fee` / `size_for_cap`. The underdog/momentum scripts live on `wip/codex-research-lab` and disappear from product checkouts.
- **Two evidence dirs are intentional:** `openterminal_paths.py` — Qt export vs app data. Do not "unify" them. Env overrides stay verbatim.
- **Drop arena means unload it:** `org.openterminal.alpha-arena` stayed loaded after the product decision. `launchctl bootout` + plist `Disabled`.
- **Cockpit FLOW lanes must not stretch:** `lane_height = flow_body / drawn` made 3–4 books look like fat cards and wasted space for COM-H/D. Paint at fixed `kLaneHeight` (24); `drawable` still uses that height for scroll capacity.
- **Bot freeze == bot refuse:** Rain freeze must use `age >= max_report_age_ms` like `KalshiBotDecision`; Auto cockpit keeps `timestamp_stale` as `age > bound`. Tick `signal_trusted` must OR all six family reports. Health chips watch present reports (not only rain columns) so empty COM-H/BTC-D cannot hide as idle; folded KPI colour is worst-of cadences.
- **Crypto scalp journal split:** Daemon `crypto-auto-scalp-v1` appends opportunity rows to `decisions.jsonl` / `scalp_state.decisions`. SPOT/SCALP cockpit proof must bind `scalp_qualification_v1.json`, not SQLite `edge crypto-recommend` (dual-source SQL still finds zero auto-scalp rows). Tape/DECIDE read state JSON.
- **Crypto right rail:** Never stack two primary green BUY CTAs (maker + full ticket) in ~290px with no scroll. One primary ticket; maker is a collapsed disclosure + outline submit; form scrolls under the book; rail ~340px. Order entry needs a hard `minimumHeight` (~360) or the book stretch swallows the ticket entirely.
- **Staged ≠ working tree:** After partial reverts / edits, always check `git diff --cached` *and* `git diff HEAD`. Inverse staged/unstaged diffs mean a commit would ship the broken index, not the good tree.
- **`translate_action` arity:** Signature is 4-arg `(choice, net_qty, edge_direction, params)`. A 3-arg call with `ActionParams{}` as 3rd arg fails to compile against current `TypedAction.h`.
- **Direction is env-owned, not LLM-owned:** `edge_direction_of` → assess/floor/`side_direction`; model only picks verb + conviction.
- **`floor_permits` in `ai ctx` is still a LONG probe** (`intent_agrees_with_edge("buy", …)`). After short entries shipped, short-endorsed edges misreport as not permitted — fix or rename (`floor_permits_long` / direction-aware).
- **`--no-floor` vs direction:** Runner floor can be skipped, but `edge_direction_of` still hard-requires full endorsement → Enter stays null without endorsed edge.
- **Research Lab + Library unity:** `_Library.cpp` and `_ResearchLab.cpp` share anon-namespace helper names; both must stay in `SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION`.
- **Paper arming:** `ai run strategy` / `ai handler run` refuse live; `StrategyRunner` submits `mode:paper`; handlers created disabled. Do not weaken these in UI work.
- **Strategies ≠ Kalshi live:** Strategies header PAPER ONLY must not host Kalshi live ARM. Arm Kalshi live only from Predictions (Kalshi). Strategies = measure/paper proof; Crypto = spot; Predictions = bet/race + live arm. Global Strategies Risk kill is separate — do not claim all kill lives only in Predictions.
- **Spot/scalp canary ≠ Kalshi arm:** Profile + Crypto cockpit arm Coinbase/Kraken canary only. Labels must say CANARY / PAPER SCALP, not LIVE ARMED / PAPER ONLY (Kalshi/Strategies vocabulary).
- **Crypto cockpit ≠ Kalshi rain:** Evolve SPOT/SCALP tab with pure `present_crypto_cockpit`; opportunity tape + DECIDE, never contract rain / COM-H. Inspect-only; arm stays Profile; kill/CLI/FAST/venues from SettingsGate.
- **Kalshi edge autopsy (2026-07-27):** Losing is often "no informational edge vs mid + fees", not bad tuning. Quote lag (~+2¢/15s after 3σ) ≈ fee after half-spread. Recalibration cannot beat raw mid. `KXBTC15M` directional tickers without strikes get dropped from outcome joins — prefer strike/threshold series (`KXBTCD`) when measuring from ticker alone; daemon snapshots still expose open as `reference_strike`/`floor_strike`.
- **Charter carve-out:** Deterministic Kalshi bot may bid only when human-armed, hard caps ($2/$3), promotion gate PASS on paper, kill switch, GUI parity. AI cannot arm live.
- **KXBTC15M vs spot_calibrator:** Hourly threshold calibrator must not own 15m race trust. Separate `kxbtc15m-calibrator.json`; `KalshiBotDecision::filter_predictions_for_family` + dual `decide` so trust cannot leak across families.
- **Multi-cadence strike families:** Commodities hourly (`KXGOLDH`/`KXSILVERH`/`KXWTIH`), daily (`KXGOLDD`/`KXSILVERD`/`KXWTI`), and BTC daily (`KXBTC`) are floor-only "above $Y" books — use `strike_threshold_family.py` OnlineLogit, not 15m Gaussian. Own reports + trust. WTI daily series ticker is `KXWTI` (not `KXWTID`). Cockpit rain tags COM-H/COM-D/BTC-D; orbit metals are GOLD/SILVER/WTI boxes with cadence folded; KPI `BTC 15M|D` / `COM 15m|H|D`; pin is **10 nodes / 6 KPI**.
- **Apples ≠ oranges (metal pooling):** Gold/Silver/Oil are different prediction problems even at the same cadence. Never authorize (or paint trusted) from a pooled Brier/trust across underlyings. Census may count apples+oranges; quality/verdict is per series. Containment (#234): multi-series reports force `adds_value_*=false` + `pooled_*` / `pooled_trust_withheld`. Split (#237): per-family model+evidence+trust before preregister/live.
- **Decide before cockpit for per-family trust:** Authorizer is `KalshiBotDecision::signal_trusted` / `family_trust`; view must mirror it, not invent it. Order: decide reads `by_family` → refuse missing → cockpit → preregister.
- **Cockpit metals are separate orbit boxes:** Row 0 = BTC 1H + BTC 15M + BRIER/SETTLEMENTS/GATE/KILL/EXPOSURE; row 1 = GOLD / SILVER / WTI with `15m|H|D` folded inside each. Never a pooled COMMODITIES 15M/1H tile. Pin **10 nodes / 6 KPI**. Colour via `family_trust` worst-of (amber > grey > green-all-pass).
- **DECIDE chips ≠ global newest:** Six orbit buckets (THR/15M/BTC-D/GOLD/SILVER/WTI) from series prefix (= `family_of` rule); newest row per bucket. One Gold BID must not paint SILVER/WTI BID. Envelope stays newest overall. Gate tile stays one node — append `gate_family_line` (`no families preregistered — admit nothing` when `!by_family_eligible` / empty). Display only; chip inspect uses `__chip_` prefix so it cannot collide with orbit `gold`/`silver`/`wti`.
- **Trust is ternary, not bool:** PASS / FAIL / UNAVAILABLE (with n). Bool collapses "Gold n=40 unmeasured" with "Gold n=200 lost to mid" — both false — and cockpit grey-as-red invites "drop commodities" when the truth is "not measured yet."
- **Python calibrators have no deploy step:** LaunchAgents run scripts from the repo path on a ~60s timer. An uncommitted working-tree edit is live immediately (state migrations / withhold can fire before merge). Never "try" producer edits in the tree expecting them to stay dark; commit/PR or edit off-path. UI PRs must not touch producers casually.
- **Cockpit additive pins:** Dual-source rain changes census (`· N threshold · M kxbtc15m`), adds `kxbtc15m` orbit node, and always appends a KXBTC15M KPI line — update `health_fields_are_additive_*` pins when those land. Metal unpool replaces pooled `commodities15m`/`commodities_hourly` orbit tiles with `gold`/`silver`/`wti` on row 1 — baseline pin is **10 nodes / 6 KPI**. Outside-info detail rides on those lines — do not add nodes without updating the pin. Commodities rain adds census `· K commodities15m` and a `COM` source tag — update rain/census pins when that lands. Bid postmortem inspect opens from the **PM KPI** (or BOT VIEW), not a new node. Always reserve the PM cell in the KPI strip so narrow widths cannot bury it under `… N more`.
- **Postmortem ≠ W/L:** Join settlements to bids by `position_id`; classify loss modes; never invent late-flip/gamma without path replay. `settle_paper` copies bid snapshot + optional `market_mid_at_settle`. Paper cashout closes with `early_exit` / `won:null`. Paper ticks attach `mid_path` when sampled. Always write **historic** + **current-rules** summaries when markers exist; cockpit/status PM judges CURRENT, not lifetime. Sealed gate still uses historic. Early exits are cashouts, not family L. GUI: Predictions BOT card + cockpit PM KPI inspect.
- **Eligible autopsy ≠ bid postmortem:** `eligible_loss_autopsy` walk-forwards threshold `resolved_record` on `|model−mid|≥edge` and reports when model Brier loses to mid (edge/runway/thesis buckets). It does not join fills. Use for trust/feature work; use `bot_bid_postmortem` for ledger PnL.
- **Paper cashout:** Sell-to-close at floor(held-side bid) only (`LOCK_WIN` / `CUT_EDGE_REVERSED` via AutoEngine). Mid is never a sell proxy. Default ON for paper; `--no-paper-cashout` disables. Hold-to-settle when HOLD or bid missing.
- **Postmortem → decide:** `FADE_YES_NEAR_CLOSE` lifts on venue-lead confirm-down **or** BRTI avg60 below open (p_brti < 0.5 when present); missing confirm → ban stands. Favourite cross asks ≥0.65 need +0.03 margin.
- **Paper KXBTCD rest-first:** Paper `threshold_rest_first` → threshold decide with `allow_cross=false` → `REST_FIRST_POLICY` even if net EV clears. Also applies to KXBTC daily. 15m race families unchanged. Opt out `--allow-threshold-cross`. Live leaves flag off.
- **Directional feature key:** Use `open_price` (not `signed_distance_bps`) to tell KXBTC15M from threshold — both families write signed distance. Commodities 15m races also carry `open_price` and fall the `open` glyph.
- **Paper pause ≠ kill switch:** Current-gen `DRAWDOWN_CAP` auto-rotates and resumes; kill switch stops the whole tick. Lifetime gate FAIL must not deadlock paper.
- **GUI rebuild ≠ CLI:** Paper LaunchAgent runs `build/openterminalcli`; rebuild CLI + kickstart (now POST_BUILD) or pause/rotate never loads.
- **Kalshi category labels:** UI `"Weather"` must fetch `"Climate and Weather"`; commodities use the real API category `"Commodities"` (KXGOLD*, KXWTI*, …).
- **Commodities 15m calibrator:** Own file `commodities-15m-calibrator.json`; reuses kxbtc15m Gaussian math; do not mix trust with BTC 15m or hourly threshold.
- **Outside-info ladder:** Observe → ablation vs mid → veto/confirm → tiny tilt → trust at n≥100. Never retune Gaussian alone expecting profit. Phase 4 blocked while `adds_value_over_market` is false.
- **Phase-4 mid-prior tilt is scored_only:** `physics_mid_prior_tilt` = mid prior × confirm-gated private LR via `capped_mid_prior_tilt` (`|Δlogit|≤0.20`). Lives in `SCORED_ABLATION_KEYS` / boards / `phase4_tilt` report on kxbtc15m + commodities15m — never in `ABLATION_KEYS` or `select_trusted_variant` until explicit promotion. Missing tilt on old obs falls back to mid (no invented LR).
- **Pyth commodities feeds:** Prefer Hermes `Metal.XAU/USD`, `Metal.XAG/USD`, `Metal.XTI/USD` for GOLD/SILVER/WTI; Yahoo is cold fallback; report settlement-parity match rate, do not invent trust from it.
- **Lag ablations are family-local:** `physics_veto_on_conflict` / `physics_confirm_only` score beside physics on kxbtc15m only; trust needs paired n≥100 vs mid; daemon persists `venue_lead_bps_30s` / `lead_conflicts` on horizon.
- **BRTI settlement underlier:** KXBTC15M pays on CF BRTI **60s average**, not last print. Daemon must parse `avg_60s_data`; calibrator ablation `physics_brti_avg60` scores that spot separately from last-print physics. Fade-ban lift may use avg60 < open.
- **Phase-3 confirms:** Futures tape (Yahoo) near close and vol/session regime are confirm/veto only — shared via `outside_info_features.py`; quiet/weekend clamps to mid.
- **FLOW HH:MM is contract close, not “as-of now”:** Rain labels parse ticker close (ET). If calibrator trusts frozen daemon `seconds_left`, closed races stay in the report and look like current FLOW. Derive `seconds_left` from ticker `close_ms` vs wall clock; refuse `now >= close`; cockpit also drops closed 15m and census-notes `N closed 15m omitted`.
- **15m rollover empty FLOW:** Daemon universe must subscribe *still-open* cohorts (not just-closed); keep ≥4 close cohorts. When WS has no open KXBTC15M snapshot, `kxbtc15m_calibrator` fills from Kalshi REST + BRTI. Stuck `universe_timeouts` → kick `org.openterminal.cli.daemon.default`.
- **Cockpit inspect is not arming:** Click on scoreboard nodes opens a read-only ablation/parity overlay; Esc/outside closes. PM KPI opens bid postmortem detail the same way. Never place/arm from the cockpit.
- **Cockpit motion is L→R:** Contract lanes are horizontal; glyphs travel left→right toward DECIDE then LEDGER. Frozen = parked (no travel). Census says `NO FLOW` / `L→R`.
- **Cockpit ambition is KXBTCD:** Rain sorts threshold first; census `threshold first · ambition KXBTCD`; pinned hero is threshold report (`KXBTCD · …`). No 7th KPI. Fallback to KXBTC15M only if strike report absent.
- **Predictions idle:** `KalshiScreen` must stop clock/evidence/dom/spot/market timers (+ spot WS reconnect) in `hideEvent`, and unsubscribe ladder market WS (resubscribe on show). Polymarket must `unsubscribe_current()` on hide. Weather `bot_timer_` must stop on hide. Lazy-construct Polymarket in `PredictionMarketsScreen`.
- **Calibrator auto-refresh:** Bot ticks kickstart LaunchAgents (or `python once`) when any family report ages past 2/3 of `max_report_age` — threshold included. Default ON; `--no-auto-refresh-calibrators` opts out. Throttle 45s/script. Does not replace LaunchAgents; prevents overnight `REPORT_STALE` stuck loops.
- **Cockpit settlements ≠ sealed gate:** SETTLEMENTS / SETTLED / NET prefer current-rules postmortem (`CUR`); SEALED GATE + HIST DD stay lifetime for live promotion. Do not paint pre-gate −$35 as the new-rules scorecard.
- **Bet-eligible trust:** `adds_value_on_bet_eligible` needs ≥100 contracts with `|model−mid|≥0.10` and better eligible Brier than mid. Population `adds_value_over_market` alone is not enough to bid.
- **Settlement window ≠ prediction:** KXBTC15M pays CF BRTI 60s average at close, not last print; commodities 15m pays Pyth 1-minute candle close (Hermes XAU/XAG/XTI), not Yahoo. Last-minute edge is observing that official statistic while `now < close` and no `result`. After REST `result` or `now >= close_ms` (ticker clock, never frozen `seconds_left`) you are late. Do not retune the race Gaussian for this.
- **GOLDH paper ≠ 15m metals:** Hourly gold strike books can beat mid on Brier while 15m GOLD/SILVER/WTI physics loses to mid. A GOLDH paper trial must stay unpooled (no silver/oil, no 15m) and hash-lock a single 10¢ executable-edge floor. Do not retune `commodities-hourly-calibrator`; do not import pre-freeze snapshots. WTI 15m Yahoo `CL=F` vs Pyth `Metal.XTI/USD` can print 0.999 vs 0.045 — that is a feed bug, not an edge.
